(Compile-fail: bug #84. `it's` sat in the keyword table as a spelling of
 `is`. It is not one, and it is the reason the contraction rule admits
 only the two spellings LANGUAGE.md documents: `it` is an ordinary
 identifier, so `print it's length.` is the possessive on a variable
 called `it` and prints a length today - see
 tests/427_apostrophe_meanings_unchanged.vox. Waking `it's` would have
 taken that possessive away.)

a number called n it's 5.
